            {
              "type": "markdown",
              "content": "**Gauge guide**\n\nGreen = manufacturer reference range. Yellow = outside that range; red = farther outside. Yellow/red transitions are dashboard attention bands, not dosing instructions or swimming-safety limits.\n\n| Reading | Green range |\n|---|---|\n| Salt | 3,000–3,500 ppm |\n| Free chlorine | 1–3 ppm |\n| pH | 7.4–7.6 |\n| Alkalinity | 80–120 ppm |\n| Stabilizer (CYA) | 50–75 ppm |\n| Calcium hardness | 175–400 ppm |\n\n[Jandy reference, sections 4.5 and 4.7](https://www.jandy.com/-/media/zodiac/global/downloads/jandy/water-sanitizers/h0325600.pdf). [Salt-pool chlorine guidance](https://support.waterguru.com/hc/en-us/articles/6469932272667-Does-the-WaterGuru-SENSE-work-in-salt-water-pools). Chlorine must be interpreted alongside CYA and sample age. Temperature and flow use neutral blue because they depend on comfort and equipment settings."
